# Hotwire & Frontend Development

## Hotwire Integration
- Use **Hotwire** (Turbo and Stimulus) for dynamic, SPA-like interactions
- Leverage Turbo Streams for real-time updates without full page reloads
- Structure HTML for optimal Turbo Frame and Stream updates

## Tailwind CSS
- Implement responsive design with **Tailwind CSS**
- Use utility-first approach for styling
- Follow mobile-first responsive design principles

## Rails Views
- Use Rails view helpers and partials to keep views DRY
- Structure templates logically with proper partials
- Use `turbo_frame_tag` and `turbo_stream_from` appropriately

## Gestor submit loaders
- Use `Buttons::SubmitLoaderComponent` for primary mutating submits (save / continue / confirm)
- The component ships `data-controller="submit-loader"` and a hidden spinner; no layout-level wiring
- Skip search / GET forms; keep custom loaders (CSV validate, freight map) as-is

## Gestor link loaders
- Use `Buttons::LinkLoaderComponent` for primary navigation CTAs (Ver / Editar / Novo / Voltar / Cancelar)
- The component ships `data-controller="link-loader"` and a hidden spinner; clears on `turbo:load`
- Skip side nav, breadcrumbs, and plain text/table name links unless they are button-styled actions

## Loading skeletons
- Use `Skeletons::Component` for loading placeholders (daisyUI-style `.skeleton` / `.skeleton-text`)
- Variants: `:block`, `:circle`, `:avatar`, `:card`, `:text`, `:table`, `:page` — or pass a custom block
- Prefer `store_lazy_skeleton_frame` on gestor CRUD index/show/form pages (lazy Turbo Frame + skeleton)
- Lazy CRUD frames use `target: "_top"` so Ver/Editar links do full-page Turbo Drive visits
- Skip the lazy frame when re-rendering forms with validation errors
- Do not replace button/link loaders with page skeletons

## Examples

### Turbo Integration
```erb
<!-- Good: Turbo Frame for partial updates -->
<%= turbo_frame_tag "user_#{user.id}" do %>
  <%= render 'user_card', user: user %>
<% end %>

<!-- Good: Turbo Stream updates -->
<%= turbo_stream_from current_user, "notifications" %>

<!-- Good: Form with Turbo -->
<%= form_with model: @user, data: { turbo_frame: "user_form" } do |f| %>
  <!-- form content -->
<% end %>
```

### Tailwind CSS Patterns
```erb
<!-- Good: Responsive design with utility classes -->
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
  <% @products.each do |product| %>
    <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow p-6">
      <%= image_tag product.image, class: "w-full h-48 object-cover rounded-md mb-4" %>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2"><%= product.name %></h3>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
```

```css
/* Good: Component-based styling */
.btn-primary {
  @apply bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-medium py-2 px-4 rounded-md;
  @apply focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2;
  @apply disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed;
}
```
